# Copy to .env (ignored by Git). Read by the local builds (build:installer, build:windows, build:linux,
# build:macos), by every app build through src-tauri/build.rs, by build:latest and build:release-data
# (the update key) and by `bun run extension:sign:firefox`. CI does not
# read it: its builds take the repository's secrets of the same names (docs/building.md, Repository secrets).
# A variable set in the environment wins over this file.

# Edge Function of feedback (supabase/README.md); the installer build does not compile without it.
KOONAPIN_FEEDBACK_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/feedback

# Public key of the Chrome Web Store draft (dashboard → Package → View public key), not a secret.
# With it `bun run extension:build` also makes release/test/chrome-edge/<version>/koonapin-chrome-store-id.zip: the extension
# with the store's id, to test Chrome and Edge against the installer build before publication.
# CHROME_STORE_PUBLIC_KEY=MIIBIjAN...

# Only for `bun run extension:sign:firefox`: the AMO API key of the owner's account
# (addons.mozilla.org → Developer Hub → Manage API Keys). Secrets; the script never prints them.
WEB_EXT_API_KEY=
WEB_EXT_API_SECRET=

# Only for `bun run build:installer -- --sign` (NP-042, Р-9): the Certum certificate in SimplySign.
# Not secrets: signing also needs SimplySign Desktop signed in with the code from SimplySign Mobile.
# Thumbprint: Get-ChildItem Cert:\CurrentUser\My -CodeSigningCert | Format-List Subject, Thumbprint
# SIGN_CERT_SHA1=
# Only if signtool.exe is neither on PATH nor in the Windows SDK folder.
# SIGNTOOL=C:\Program Files (x86)\Windows Kits\10\bin\10.0.26100.0\x64\signtool.exe

# Only for `bun run build:latest` and `bun run build:release-data` (NP-038, Р-60): the update key of NP-042,
# encrypted by its password.
# The password here, or in the shell for the run if it should not lie on the disk.
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=C:\Users\<you>\.tauri\koonapin.key
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=

# Sync between computers (commercial/sync, Р-68): the relay's WebSocket address. Without it a build
# has no sync. CI takes it from the secret of the same name.
# KOONAPIN_SYNC_URL=wss://<the relay>/v1/sync

# macOS signing and notarization (scripts/build-macos.mjs, NP-051). The Developer ID Application identity
# as `security find-identity -v -p codesigning` prints it, and an App Store Connect API key (Users and
# Access → Integrations → Team Keys, role Developer): its Issuer ID, Key ID and the path of its .p8,
# kept outside the repository. Without them build:macos is signed ad hoc and has no Safari extension.
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY=
APPLE_API_ISSUER=
APPLE_API_KEY=
APPLE_API_KEY_PATH=
# The App Store build (scripts/build-ios.mjs, NP-078) signs and uploads with a key of its own, kept on
# the build Mac and never in CI: Xcode's cloud-managed distribution certificate needs the Admin role (a
# Developer key fails with «Cloud signing permission error»). Its Issuer ID, Key ID and the path of its
# .p8. The team's ten-character Team ID; without it the team in APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY's parentheses.
APPLE_STORE_ISSUER=
APPLE_STORE_KEY=
APPLE_STORE_KEY_PATH=
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# Only for `bun run ci:secrets APPLE_` (the CI's copy of the certificate): the .p12 exported from Keychain
# Access with its private key, outside the repository, and its password. Delete both once the secrets are set.
APPLE_CERTIFICATE_PATH=
APPLE_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD=

# Google Play's upload key (scripts/build-android.mjs, NP-074a): a PKCS12 keystore kept outside the
# repository and never in CI, its password (the key's too) and the key's alias. Play signs what it delivers
# with the app signing key it generates and keeps (docs/building.md); no build has that key. build:android
# signs with the upload key only a clean commit of origin/main (or a test with --sign-test), else with the
# debug key.
ANDROID_UPLOAD_KEYSTORE=
ANDROID_UPLOAD_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=
ANDROID_UPLOAD_KEY_ALIAS=
# bundletool-all-<version>.jar (github.com/google/bundletool/releases): build:android validates the App
# Bundle with it, as Play Console does on upload. Required for a build for Play.
BUNDLETOOL=
